WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.895
In under two minutes, you will control voting: pause it, check the votes, and void a bad one.

00:00:05.895 --> 00:00:07.064
We start on the map.

00:00:07.969 --> 00:00:11.301
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:15.600
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.090
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.436
Tap Use my location.

00:00:21.181 --> 00:00:23.397
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:23.397 --> 00:00:24.049
Tap Allow.

00:00:27.605 --> 00:00:30.100
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.318
See the three dots?

00:00:31.318 --> 00:00:31.866
Tap them.

00:00:33.468 --> 00:00:35.431
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:37.124 --> 00:00:37.752
Tap Mine.

00:00:37.752 --> 00:00:39.701
These are the contests you run.

00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:43.399
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:44.767
This is your dashboard.

00:00:46.652 --> 00:00:48.998
Voting opens and closes on your dates.

00:00:48.998 --> 00:00:51.343
The Controls card lets you change that.

00:00:52.244 --> 00:00:54.776
Tap Pause voting to stop votes for a moment.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:00:58.448
Tap Resume voting to start again.

00:01:00.251 --> 00:01:02.216
Tap Results for the full tally.

00:01:02.216 --> 00:01:05.592
You always see the counts, even when the public cannot.

00:01:07.396 --> 00:01:09.479
Open Review individual votes.

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:11.215
Odd patterns are flagged.

00:01:13.247 --> 00:01:15.732
Tap Void next to a vote that should not count.

00:01:17.612 --> 00:01:20.793
Next up: Add co-organizers and judges.
